.TH FAMILY-CONNECT 1 "2026-10-28" "family-connect 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
family-connect \- family chat and calls on the family's own server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B family-connect
.br
.B family-connect
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B family-connect
is the Linux client of Family Connect, a chat for one household, or several,
on a server the family runs itself. Every family has one chat for all its
members, and any two members can talk one to one: messages, photos, videos,
voice notes, files, locations and polls, one-to-one voice and video calls, a
family board and birthdays.
.PP
Family Connect runs as a single instance per session: a second
.B family-connect
brings the running one's window forward and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apparmor.d/family-connect
The AppArmor profile that lets WebKit's sandbox start on Ubuntu.
.SH AUTHOR
nettrash <nettrash@nettrash.me>
.SH SEE ALSO
https://nettrash.me/linux/familyconnect/support.html
